# An MP4 file as a video's src, played by the element itself: the file is
# read whole (the tables, the H.264 configuration, every sample), its size
# and length told, H.264 and AAC both said to be playable, the pictures
# decoded on the machine's hardware in decode order (B pictures lean on
# later ones) and shown by their presentation time, and the element ends
# at the file's end. The test picture's colour bars give the pixels (the
# page starts under the window's 78 px of chrome): red at (20, 62) and
# blue at (80, 112) of the picture, as ffmpeg decodes it.
require-video-hardware h264
resize 320 200
open video-mp4.html
advance 10 10
assert-title MP4 160x120 1.00s probably/probably b0.000-1.000 r4
advance 100
assert-pixel 20 140 #ff0000
assert-pixel 80 190 #0000ff
assert-pixel 300 150 #222244
advance 100 12
assert-title MP4 ended at 1.00
